# Data conversion between bit and mebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between bit and mebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1b to 0.0000MiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5b yields 0.0000MiB; backward, converting 1MiB to 8388608b preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5MiB yields 12582912.0b. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1b
print(forward_whole->to(MiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5b
print(forward_fractional->to(MiB))
backward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(backward_whole->to(b))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(backward_fractional->to(b))

<<< stdout
0.0000MiB
0.0000MiB
8388608b
12582912.0b

<<< stderr
